        "procedure": "A mixture of Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.2 mmol, 0.09 g) and 9-anthracenecarboxylic acid (HAC; 0.45 mmol, 0.10 g) was dissolved in 5 ml of CH3OH and 5 ml of CH3CN. The resultant solution with 0.20 ml CH3NH2 was added in a Teflon-lined autoclave (20 ml) and placed in an oven at 120 °C to react for 5 days. Orange X-ray-quality crystals were obtained and dried in air.",
